### FilmFuse core-api - profile endpoints
# Get a token: sign in via the client, or against local Supabase:
#   curl -s -X POST 'http://127.0.0.1:54321/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password' \
#     -H "apikey: <anon key from `supabase status`>" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"email":"you@example.com","password":"..."}' | jq -r .access_token
# Then set @token below (never commit a real one).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-access-token-here

### Health (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Current profile (auto-provisioned on first call)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update profile (partial; null/omitted = unchanged, "" clears displayName/bio; photo: see profile-photo.http)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "movie_buff",
  "displayName": "Movie Buff",
  "bio": "Horror on weekdays, rom-coms on Sundays."
}

### Invalid username -> 400 with fieldErrors
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "no spaces!"
}

### Complete onboarding (interim: needs a username; idempotent, keeps the first timestamp)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/onboarding/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Username availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/usernames/movie_buff/available
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me

### Delete account -> 204 (profile row, photo, Supabase Auth user). Irreversible!
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
